# The algebraic properties an operation may satisfy, the laws that distinguish one structure from another. The core
# ones, in the order the number tower loses them going up: totality of an order (lost past the integers, where a square
# root of minus one appears with a square below zero), commutativity (lost at the quaternions), associativity (lost at
# the octonions, leaving only alternativity, where any two elements generate an associative subalgebra), and the
# multiplicative norm (lost at the sedenions, where zero divisors appear). Each property is a universal equation over an
# operation; the machine-checked instances over the integers (commutativity, associativity, distributivity) live in the
# number files, and the tower's losses are recorded in the algebra-tower files.
